# Line endings.
#
# The team develops on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which is fine for
# source that only ever runs through a toolchain. It is not fine for the files
# that are executed by a Linux shell inside a container: a shell script with
# CRLF endings fails with `syntax error: unexpected "|"`, because the carriage
# return is part of the token. The backup runner met exactly that.
#
# So: normalise everything in the repository, and pin the files that Linux
# executes to LF in the working tree as well.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
